# This file was rewritten on 2026-09-09. It had been left holding an assistant's
# own reasoning text ("Wait, let me reconsider this...") wrapped in markdown
# fences, so line 52 was a literal ``` pattern and the prose lines were patterns
# that matched nothing. The real patterns below survived that; the gaps did not.

# Scan output. starreckon_corpus.jsonl is a REAL corpus of this machine's
# sessions — session ids, model names, token counts, dates. It is 4.8 MB of
# personal telemetry sitting in the repo root of a public repository, and it was
# not ignored. A single `git add -A` would have published it, which is the exact
# thing this tool exists to prevent.
starreckon_corpus.jsonl
*_corpus.jsonl
starreckon-*.tgz

